    {
      "id": "12fcb19fe41d19729101d0cc5be7259cf32a3714",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 675815569,
          "type": null,
          "body": "There seems to be two changes merged into one here. The underlying categorizing change, as well as this \"Jackpot\" mode. I do not necessarily see the need for such a mode, especially as it is a compile switch, but keeping that aside for a second, I have an issue here, that possibly legitimate changes are merged together with a special one. Therefore I would much rather prefer those two things to be splitted up.\n\nOn the jackpot mode itself, I have another issue with code, that by default won't be build. This will lead to a scenario, where in the near future, the underlying code may change and this one does not leading to code that no longer works. At the very least, the switch should be a cmake option and not a compiler definition.\n\nSo for now, I would prefer if this code does NOT get merged as-is",
          "author": {
            "id": 2498449,
            "username": "rknall",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Roland Knall",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/9e1d973c5007651b2ca47071f80324c2de5349d873e365cf0761df5542dfe382?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/rknall"
          },
          "created_at": "2021-09-13T10:33:08.179Z",
          "updated_at": "2021-09-13T10:33:08.179Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 116458006,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": false,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 4170,
          "commands_changes": {}
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "7e260eab4fc211f3ffd670e65f5f623d15e87d3a",
      "individual_note": false,
      "resolvable": true,
      "resolved": true,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 675830523,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "Fair comments, and similar to thoughts that had crossed my mind while coding.  I tend to try to avoid using `#define` for code blocks too... it tends to lead to \"code rot\".  But the comment said a \"define\", so that's what I did.  :stuck_out_tongue_winking_eye: \n\nBut I don't understand how using a cmake option would help, other than perhaps through facilitating easier automation of builds (or even easier manual builds) to ensure that the code continues to be compilable in future.  Is that the goal?  (That's a genuine \"I don't understand\", not at all a challenge to the idea.)\n\nIn the meantime, I shall minimize this change down to introducing `ct_conversation_trace_type_t` and the other non-jackpot-related preparatory restructuring, if that sounds agreeable.",
          "author": {
            "id": 7889756,
            "username": "dariusd0",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "dariusd0",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/f0f4a609abaf984c9cfe277f1321b8db104aea7290fcbb7fb0c5749a00d32e39?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/dariusd0"
          },
          "created_at": "2021-09-13T10:47:44.666Z",
          "updated_at": "2021-09-13T11:06:28.129Z",
