        },
        {
          "id": 675849769,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "> But I don't understand how using a cmake option would help, other than perhaps through facilitating easier automation of builds (or even easier manual builds) to ensure that the code continues to be compilable in future.\n\nYeah, that was the idea behind the cmake-switch, just to make it easier to compile the code and perhaps allow for adding a gitlab-ci step testing compatibility (although I don't know about that).\n\n> In the meantime, I shall minimize this change down to introducing `ct_conversation_trace_type_t` and the other non-jackpot-related preparatory restructuring, if that sounds agreeable.\n\nThat would be great",
